<div class="sa-shell">
  <header class="sa-section">
    <h1>Scene Architect</h1>
    <p>Build architecture locally. Generate appearance, inspect the composite, then create a playable scene.</p>
    <ol class="sa-progress" aria-label="Scene creation progress">
      {{#each steps}}
      <li class="sa-progress-item {{#if current}}is-current{{/if}} {{#if complete}}is-complete{{/if}}" data-step="{{number}}" {{#if current}}aria-current="step"{{/if}}>
        <span class="sa-progress-index">{{number}}</span><span>{{label}}</span>
      </li>
      {{/each}}
    </ol>
    <p class="sa-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-status>{{status}}</p>
    {{#if partialScene}}<p role="alert">Partial scene {{partialScene}} remains after cleanup failed. It is NOT complete. Inspect or delete that scene manually.</p>{{/if}}
    <details>
      <summary>Saved projects</summary>
      <label>Project <select name="projectId"><option value="">Choose a saved scene</option>{{#each projects}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
      <div class="sa-actions"><button type="button" data-action="reopen">Reopen project</button><button type="button" data-action="newProject">New local project</button></div>
      <p class="hint">A validated local plan is saved on this client. Local image files are not saved until scene creation/update; reselect unsaved files after closing.</p>
    </details>
  </header>

  <section class="sa-section" aria-labelledby="sa-describe-title">
    <h2 id="sa-describe-title">1. Describe</h2>
    <div class="sa-grid sa-grid-4">
      <label>Scene name <input name="sceneName" type="text" value="{{sceneName}}"></label>
      <label>Columns <input name="columns" type="number" min="4" step="1" value="{{columns}}"></label>
      <label>Rows <input name="rows" type="number" min="4" step="1" value="{{rows}}"></label>
      <label>Grid pixels <input name="gridSize" type="number" min="50" step="1" value="{{gridSize}}"></label>
    </div>
    <label>Scene description <textarea name="brief" rows="3" placeholder="Rooms, circulation, major features, mood and lighting">{{brief}}</textarea></label>
    <p class="hint">Copy the design request to a language model, then import its coordinate-free JSON. Or start with the laboratory example. Editing this description does not silently change built geometry.</p>
    <div class="sa-actions sa-wrap">
      <button type="button" data-action="copyLayoutPrompt" class="{{#if next.copyLayoutPrompt}}sa-primary{{/if}}">Copy scene design request</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="pastePlan" class="{{#if next.pastePlan}}sa-primary{{/if}}">Import scene design</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="loadExample">Load laboratory example</button>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>Advanced: low-level plan import and repair</summary>
      <p>Import exact coordinates only if needed. Validation is atomic: rejected JSON never replaces a valid plan. Accepted changes start a local project, preserving any saved scene.</p>
      <div class="sa-actions sa-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-action="copyLegacyLayoutPrompt">Copy low-level plan request</button>
        <button type="button" data-action="pastePlan" data-mode="advanced">Import / edit low-level plan</button>
        {{#if hasPlan}}<button type="button" data-action="downloadPlan">Download plan JSON</button>{{/if}}
      </div>
      {{#if planRepair}}<p role="alert">Advanced plan not accepted: {{planRepair.error}}</p><button type="button" data-action="copyPlanRepairPrompt">Copy plan correction request</button><pre>{{planRepair.json}}</pre>{{/if}}
      {{#if hasPlan}}<pre>{{planJson}}</pre>{{/if}}
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="sa-section" aria-labelledby="sa-build-title">
    <h2 id="sa-build-title">2. Build</h2>
    <p>{{#if hasPlan}}{{planSummary}}{{else}}Import a design to construct deterministic rooms, passages and major feature regions.{{/if}}</p>
    <button type="button" data-action="buildPlan" class="{{#if next.buildPlan}}sa-primary{{/if}}" {{#unless hasPlan}}disabled{{/unless}}>Build local preview</button>
    <p class="hint">No Foundry scene is created here. Walls, interactive doors and light positions come only from this plan.</p>
    {{#each warnings}}<p class="sa-status warning">{{this}}</p>{{/each}}
    <div class="sa-plan-preview"></div>
    {{#if hasPlan}}
    <details>
      <summary>Advanced rendering controls</summary>
      <p>These affect structural appearance, not native geometry. Changing them invalidates the handoff and artwork preview.</p>
      <div class="sa-grid sa-grid-3">
        <label>Structural material <select name="material" data-rendering><option value="{{settings.material}}" selected>{{settings.material}} (current)</option><option value="stone">Stone</option><option value="wood">Wood</option><option value="metal">Metal</option></select></label>
        <label>Wall width (cells) <input name="wallWidth" data-rendering type="number" min="0.08" max="0.35" step="0.01" value="{{settings.wallWidth}}"></label>
        <label>Protected band padding (cells) <input name="bandPadding" data-rendering type="number" min="0.1" max="0.65" step="0.01" value="{{settings.bandPadding}}"></label>
      </div>
      <button type="button" data-action="applyRendering">Apply rendering settings</button>
    </details>
    {{/if}}
  </section>

  <section class="sa-section" aria-labelledby="sa-generate-title">
    <h2 id="sa-generate-title">3. Generate Artwork</h2>
    <p>One handoff action downloads the reference PNG and copies its prompt. Attach the PNG and prompt to your preferred multimodal image model. No model account or API is connected here.</p>
    <button type="button" data-action="handoff" class="{{#if next.handoff}}sa-primary{{/if}}" {{#unless built}}disabled{{/unless}}>Download reference + copy artwork prompt</button>
    <div data-handoff-text>
      {{#if handoffPrompt}}<details open><summary>Artwork prompt — also available if clipboard access failed</summary><label>Prompt text <textarea readonly rows="8">{{handoffPrompt}}</textarea></label><button type="button" data-action="downloadPrompt">Download artwork prompt</button></details>{{/if}}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sa-section" aria-labelledby="sa-import-title">
    <h2 id="sa-import-title">4. Import Artwork</h2>
    <label>Complete artwork image <input name="mapFile" type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp" {{#unless built}}disabled{{/unless}}></label>
    <p data-selected-file>{{#if selectedName}}Selected: {{selectedName}}{{else}}No local file selected; saved original source will be used if available.{{/if}}</p>
    {{#if mapSource}}<p class="sa-path">Original source: {{mapSource}}</p>{{/if}}
    {{#if legacySource}}<p class="sa-status warning">Legacy source: old stretch, crop and offset metadata will not be reused. This original image must pass the new full-frame aspect-ratio check.</p>{{/if}}
    <p class="hint">PNG, JPEG or WebP, up to 30 MB and 40 megapixels. Incompatible aspect ratios are rejected, never stretched or cropped. Protected bands are replaced; native geometry never follows pixels.</p>
    <div class="sa-actions"><button type="button" data-action="previewArtwork" class="{{#if next.previewArtwork}}sa-primary{{/if}}" {{#unless built}}disabled{{/unless}}>Preview artwork composite</button><button type="button" data-action="cancelPreview" {{#unless hasPreview}}disabled{{/unless}}>Cancel preview</button></div>
    <div class="sa-artwork-preview"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="sa-section" aria-labelledby="sa-create-title">
    <h2 id="sa-create-title">5. Create / Update Scene</h2>
    {{#if conflict}}<p class="sa-status warning" role="alert">{{conflict}}</p>{{/if}}
    <label class="sa-check"><input type="checkbox" name="artworkReviewed" {{#unless hasPreview}}disabled{{/unless}}>I inspected this exact composite: entrances are clear and major features are acceptable.</label>
    <div class="sa-actions sa-wrap">
      {{#if sceneReady}}
      <button type="button" data-action="updateScene" data-commit class="{{#if next.updateScene}}sa-primary{{/if}}" {{#unless canUpdate}}disabled{{/unless}}>Update Scene artwork only</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="createNewScene" data-commit class="{{#if next.createNewScene}}sa-primary{{/if}}" {{#unless hasPreview}}disabled{{/unless}}>Create NEW Scene from original plan</button>
      {{else}}
      <button type="button" data-action="createScene" data-commit class="{{#if next.createScene}}sa-primary{{/if}}" {{#unless hasPreview}}disabled{{/unless}}>Create Scene</button>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    <p class="hint">Source and exact preview PNG are uploaded before scene creation. Updating replaces only the background; door states, native lights, walls and user content remain unchanged.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sa-section" aria-labelledby="sa-play-title">
    <h2 id="sa-play-title">6. Play</h2>
    <button type="button" data-action="viewScene" class="{{#if next.viewScene}}sa-primary{{/if}}" {{#unless sceneReady}}disabled{{/unless}}>Open Scene for play</button>
    <p>In Foundry, test token vision, door interactions, wall occlusion and lighting. Artwork quality and major-feature placement still require your judgement.</p>
  </section>
  {{#if hasPlan}}
  <details class="sa-section">
    <summary>Optional diagnostics — one view at a time</summary>
    <label>Diagnostic view <select name="diagnosticView"><option value="geometry">Geometry only</option><option value="protected">Protected structural mask</option><option value="anchors">Major-anchor mask</option><option value="source">Original source</option><option value="composite">Composite</option></select></label>
    <button type="button" data-action="showDiagnostic">Show diagnostic</button>
    <p class="hint">Diagnostics do not alter the clean primary preview. No combined wall/light overlay is used.</p>
    <div class="sa-diagnostic-preview"></div>
  </details>
  {{/if}}
</div>
